  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nHot and mostly dry summer weather should stick around for the \nforeseeable future. Isolated seabreeze showers remain possible each \nafternoon and early evening over the Coastal Plains and eastern I-35 \ncorridor, but those chances will start to diminish as ridging \nintensifies over our area during the week. Warmer mid-level air \nassociated with this strengthened ridging is expected to arrive \naround Tuesday and suppress opportunities for rain from then onward.\n\nDaytime highs are forecast to inch up some as the warmest of this \nair expands across South Central Texas mid to late week. Ambient \ntemperatures during this stretch are forecast to reach the 100-102F \nrange for many areas each day. Apparent temperatures with Gulf \nmoisture staying in place could necessitate Heat Advisories later in \nthe week as values above 108F are possible across areas mainly east \nof I-37/I-35. The outlook for the upcoming weekend and through mid \nAugust looks quite dry and hot at this range without much indication \nin ensemble guidance that ridging will move out of the area.",
